---
/**
 * The problem, stated once and quietly: type only, no figures. "lost" is drawn
 * as a dashed outline, the drafting convention for a hidden line.
 */
---

<section class="problem" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
  <div class="container grid problem__grid">
    <h2 id="problem-title" class="problem__title">
      Design intent gets <span class="problem__hidden">lost</span> between revisions.
    </h2>
    <p class="problem__text">
      Why did the wall get thicker? When did the material change? Trace keeps every change with its
      value before and after, so reviews, handoffs and audits start from the full record.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .problem {
    padding-block: var(--sp-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }

  .problem__grid {
    row-gap: var(--sp-3);
    align-items: end;
  }

  .problem__title,
  .problem__text {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .problem__title {
    font-size: clamp(var(--s4), 1.1rem + 3.2vw, 3.75rem);
    font-weight: 780;
    font-stretch: 114%;
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  /* Outline only, broken into dashes by a diagonal mask: a hidden line. */
  .problem__hidden {
    color: transparent;
    -webkit-text-stroke: 2px var(--text-strong);
    -webkit-mask-image: repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg, #000 0 5px, transparent 5px 8px);
    mask-image: repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg, #000 0 5px, transparent 5px 8px);
  }

  @supports not (-webkit-text-stroke: 1px black) {
    .problem__hidden {
      color: var(--text-faint);
    }
  }

  .problem__text {
    max-width: 44ch;
    font-size: var(--s1);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .problem__title {
      grid-column: 1 / span 11;
    }

    .problem__text {
      grid-column: 12 / -1;
      font-size: var(--s0);
    }
  }
</style>
